### Automatic Bandwidth for MPLS-TE and SR-TE
**Presenter**: Rakesh Gandhi  
**Slides**: [2.1 Automatic Bandwidth for MPLS-TE and SR-TE](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-pce-21-automatic-bandwidth-for-mpls-te-and-sr-te-00)  
**Draft**: `draft-ietf-pce-stateful-pce-autobw-update`

* **Updates**: The draft extends RFC 8733 to support SR-TE (SR-MPLS and SRv6), multipath LSPs (per-path attribute lists), and adds a mechanism allowing a zero value to signal resetting an attribute to default.
* **Discussion**:
  * Dhruv Dhody confirmed that this draft will hold the baseline RBNF grammar referenced by related performance measurement drafts.
  * Adrian Farrell raised an RBNF syntax question regarding whether `attribute list` allows empty definitions.
  * Samuel Sidor and Rakesh Gandhi agreed to coordinate on RBNF refinements on the mailing list.
* **Outcome**: Document is ready for Working Group Last Call once the RBNF details are finalized on the list.

