### PCEP Extensions for LSP Validation
**Presenter**: Marina Koldobsky  
**Slides**: [2.3 PCEP extensions for LSP validation](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-pce-23-pcep-extensions-for-lsp-validation-02)

* **Overview**: Proposes allowing PCInitiated LSPs to be instantiated in a downstate when validation or resource allocation fails (e.g., missing binding label/SID, ERO resolution failure, or SBFD resource constraints) so they can automatically become active when network conditions change.
* **Discussion**: Samuel Sidor suggested introducing a generic capability flag for creating LSPs in downstate rather than fine-grained per-use-case capability bits, keeping the implementation future-proof. Samuel Sidor and Marina Koldobsky agreed to collaborate on updating the proposal.

