### PCEP over QUIC
**Presenter**: Li Feng  
**Slides**: [3.2 PCEP over QUIC](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-pce-32-pcep-over-quic-00)

* **Overview**: Explores running PCEP over QUIC to prevent single-PST failures from tearing down an entire session and to address head-of-line blocking via per-PST streams and stream prioritization.
* **Discussion**:
  * Andrew Stone expressed skepticism regarding the benefit for PCE-to-PCC sessions given low data volumes, and cautioned that interweaving prioritized messages could cause out-of-order state processing logic errors. He noted potential value for PCE-to-PCE state synchronization (`draft-ietf-pce-pcep-state-sync`).
  * Dhruv Dhody noted that adding transport complexity requires strong justification, referencing recent Transport/WIT area guidance questioning QUIC for control-plane router protocols.
  * Ketan Talaulikar advised thorough due diligence, noting BGP and PCEP have distinct characteristics.

